      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The scientific consensus is that biological sex and gender identity are distinct concepts, with sex generally determined at birth based on chromosomal and anatomical characteristics and gender being an internal sense of self. Research indicates that while a strong majority of transgender individuals exhibit a clear and consistent sense of gender from a young age, this experience is highly individual and not a matter of \"choice.\" It is also important to note that being transgender is not considered a mental illness, but rather a normal variation of human diversity.",
